You are reviewing whether the target project's own guidance, already gathered below, is sufficient for this task — or whether something relevant is missing or contradictory. Return only valid JSON with this schema: {"status": "sufficient"|"missing"|"conflicting", "requires_review": boolean, "summary": string, "related_locations": [string], "proposed_change": string, "reason": string}.

Set status to "sufficient" when the guidance below already covers what this task needs, or when the task does not depend on any project-specific rule, pattern, or convention at all — most tasks fall here. Set status to "missing" only when the task clearly depends on a project-specific rule, pattern, or convention that nothing below covers. Set status to "conflicting" only when the guidance below contains statements that contradict each other on something relevant to this task. Set requires_review to true only when the gap or conflict actually matters for doing this task safely or correctly; many tasks can proceed fine on incomplete project guidance, and requires_review must stay false in that case — conflicting guidance always requires review regardless of what you set here. related_locations must name the existing file(s) or section(s) discovered below that relate to the gap or conflict, or an empty list if nothing related exists in the project yet. proposed_change must be the smallest concrete addition (for example one new bullet, or one new small skill file) that would resolve the gap — never propose rewriting or restructuring existing guidance, and never state the new rule's content as if it were already decided; only describe where it should go. Do not invent the rule's substance yourself.

